# ____title____
#
# A talk with slides. `pnpm build` says it and films the deck in index.html.
# A mark goes on the line before the words it belongs with:
#
#   [slide how]           show the slide the page calls `how`
#   [slide how step:2]    reveal its steps up to 2
#
# A step for every line that is spoken reads best: what is being said is what just arrived.
#   [speakers ...]        what is drawn of whoever speaks: faces, lower-third, waveform, captions
#
@characters
NARRATOR: { persona: narrator, name: ____fullName____, title: ____role____ }
---
[speakers lower-third captions]
[slide title]
NARRATOR: Hello. This is a talk that was written down, not recorded.
[slide how]
NARRATOR: Three things make it.
[slide how step:1]
NARRATOR: A script says the words, and when the slides change.
[slide how step:2]
NARRATOR: A page holds the slides.
[slide how step:3]
NARRATOR: And the engine says the script, then films the page as it follows along.
[slide moves]
NARRATOR: Nothing on a slide has to just appear.
[slide moves step:1]
NARRATOR: A word in the page says how each thing arrives: from the left, wiped across, or drawn like a line.
[slide moves step:2]
NARRATOR: And what a page draws for itself, like these bars, it draws by the script's clock, so the film and the preview agree.
[slide marks]
[speakers waveform captions]
NARRATOR: Everything that happens on the screen is a mark in the script, on the line before the words it goes with.
[pause 0.4]
[slide close]
[speakers captions]
NARRATOR: Change the words, change the slides, and film it again.
